Just a great time with the game.

01:03:56.860 --> 01:03:57.780
Very chill, cozy.

01:03:58.560 --> 01:04:01.820
I really did not enjoy playing this on the NES.

01:04:01.820 --> 01:04:15.680
Now, I know Joe mentioned about the select hotkeys, and I agree that that was a welcome thing because it would have been really bad to have to, you know, constantly go down to the lower half of the screen and select your action.

01:04:16.240 --> 01:04:24.680
However, I just couldn't stop thinking about how much better this game must be with a mouse and keyboard to the point where I eventually just played it with a mouse and keyboard.

01:04:25.460 --> 01:04:31.860
Sure, the graphics are also better on the computer games, but I didn't think it was like, apparently, like, a lot of people hate the NES style.

01:04:32.060 --> 01:04:33.900
Like, I didn't think it was that bad or anything.

01:04:33.960 --> 01:04:43.440
I'm not keeping this off my, I'm not changing my vote to a no because of anything other than just the fact that I didn't like playing this with an NES controller.

01:04:43.440 --> 01:04:55.120
You give me a mouse and keyboard, this game still holds up no problem in 2025, but I can't in good faith put the NES version on our NES essential games list.

01:04:55.260 --> 01:05:01.540
And so I'm going to say no, but I won't be surprised to see a Shadowgate situation where this is on the list anyway.

01:05:02.140 --> 01:05:05.560
Sean? No, I actually kind of agree with you here.

01:05:06.820 --> 01:05:10.240
I at no point really had that.

01:05:10.360 --> 01:05:23.440
I was always charmed by the game, but maybe this is making me think about things and decisions made and about reasons for putting games on lists.

01:05:24.860 --> 01:05:28.920
Because that's exactly my, that was exactly my thought.

01:05:28.920 --> 01:05:41.760
Like, I wanted to play Day of the Tentacle because part of it's like, oh, it's this, but it's also like, it's, it, like, I can play it with the, with the input device that it's meant to be played with.

01:05:42.020 --> 01:05:54.760
Like, I remember I bought Myst on PS1 and I just could not, I could not abide by just using, like, a D-pad and some buttons.

01:05:54.760 --> 01:06:02.900
Like, I think that this is now me kind of mea culpa-ing Shadowgate in a way.

01:06:03.600 --> 01:06:09.160
Because again, both great games, but they are definitely not the perfect way to play them.

01:06:09.300 --> 01:06:11.360
So yeah, I'm going to, I'm going to keep it off as well.

01:06:11.840 --> 01:06:15.600
Joe, you can't put it on, but you could put it on your personal essential games list.

01:06:15.740 --> 01:06:18.740
What is your vote? Well, I'm crushed.

01:06:19.700 --> 01:06:21.400
But yeah, I'm voting this essential.

01:06:21.620 --> 01:06:23.300
Like, absolutely. I had so much fun with this.

01:06:23.320 --> 01:06:24.840
And I get what you're, what you guys are both saying.

01:06:24.880 --> 01:06:31.940
I mean, absolutely. This is clearly, like, would be a little more, would be more comfortable with a mouse, with a mouse and keyboard, I guess.

01:06:32.120 --> 01:06:33.100
Or just a mouse. Yeah.

01:06:33.600 --> 01:06:35.700
You wouldn't need the keyboard, actually, now that I'm asking it.

01:06:35.880 --> 01:06:36.900
I guess, I guess you wouldn't.

01:06:37.060 --> 01:06:41.400
But, but like, to me, it's just like not that big of a deal.

01:06:41.400 --> 01:06:46.580
It's not like I'm using, it's not like it's like a mouse where I'm like moving through 3D spam, just moving a cursor around the thing.

01:06:46.700 --> 01:06:51.940
So it's like, I agree that like it would be better that way, but like, I haven't played it that way to even compare it.

01:06:52.140 --> 01:07:03.020
And the amount of fun that I had with this game and like how impressed I was with everything you can do, how much this game is working in the background, all the different paths you can go on, the multiple endings.

01:07:03.020 --> 01:07:15.940
I mean, I mean, like, I'm itching to play this again and try a different ending and try, you know, doing things that, you know, I didn't complete last time and seeing all the things that I can do other, you know, other ways.

01:07:15.940 --> 01:07:27.120
And maybe I will try it on the, on the PC, but like, just don't know if just the lack of that mouse is like enough of a difference to say like, yeah, this is not an essential NES game.

01:07:27.120 --> 01:07:30.160
I think that, or like an essential game, like play this game.

01:07:30.320 --> 01:07:36.700
If you have an NES, like, I don't think you'll, at least I don't regret playing this on the NES.

01:07:36.900 --> 01:07:38.740
Like, I like. Well, I wouldn't say it's regret.

01:07:38.960 --> 01:07:40.340
Not enough. What's that?

01:07:40.480 --> 01:07:42.720
I don't know if it's regret is what we would describe it as well.

01:07:42.720 --> 01:07:44.600
Well, yeah, I'm not saying you guys regret it.

01:07:44.740 --> 01:07:52.080
I'm just, I'm just saying like playing it on the NES was a blast for me, regardless of like the, the, the inconvenience of using the D-pad.

01:07:52.400 --> 01:07:53.940
It just wasn't that big of a deal to me.

01:07:53.940 --> 01:08:00.680
So like everything else about this game was head and shoulders, like in the essential for me.

01:08:00.760 --> 01:08:02.580
So I, I got to stick with essential.

01:08:03.420 --> 01:08:04.680
Yeah, I think that's fair, Joe.

01:08:04.800 --> 01:08:12.880
And I also think, you know, you're hitting something correct there, which is a lot of, as I was saying in the episode, like, I don't think a lot of people experience this on computers first.

01:08:12.880 --> 01:08:19.660
Like, I think the NES entry was their, you know, even their gateway to point and click games at all, right?

01:08:19.660 --> 01:08:22.420
Like they might not have ever played a point and click computer game.

01:08:22.560 --> 01:08:27.520
And so, uh, maniac mansion opened that world for them with the NES controller.

01:08:27.660 --> 01:08:28.800
And that's what they had.

01:08:28.940 --> 01:08:31.380
Uh, obviously Sean and I aren't arguing that.

01:08:31.380 --> 01:08:41.680
And I think it's funny that somehow we've kept, uh, maniac mansion, which, uh, you know, I had a blast with off the essential games list while we're all agreeing that it is a great game.

01:08:41.680 --> 01:08:43.560
I stand by what I said, though.

01:08:44.360 --> 01:08:49.700
